1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,356
Day 59: Heretic, an open-source tool that removes a model's

2
00:00:04,356 --> 00:00:07,530
refusal behavior with no retraining at all,

3
00:00:07,530 --> 00:00:09,671
tested on a CPU-only machine.

4
00:00:10,121 --> 00:00:14,136
Heretic finds the direction inside a model's activations that

5
00:00:14,136 --> 00:00:17,822
triggers refusals, then lets Optuna tune how strongly to

6
00:00:17,822 --> 00:00:18,480
remove it.

7
00:00:18,930 --> 00:00:21,985
ARA compares harmless and harmful prompts and

8
00:00:21,985 --> 00:00:25,922
extracts one residual-stream direction that corresponds to

9
00:00:25,922 --> 00:00:26,465
refusal.

10
00:00:26,915 --> 00:00:29,668
Optuna searches how strongly and in which

11
00:00:29,668 --> 00:00:31,816
layers to remove that direction,

12
00:00:31,816 --> 00:00:34,032
every trial running on plain CPU.

13
00:00:34,482 --> 00:00:36,938
Each trial is scored on refusal rate and

14
00:00:36,938 --> 00:00:39,271
KL divergence from the original model,

15
00:00:39,271 --> 00:00:42,156
and the best trade-off becomes the final model.

16
00:00:42,606 --> 00:00:47,791
On Qwen3-0.6B, baseline refusal rate was 6 out of 20.

17
00:00:47,791 --> 00:00:52,583
After 12 Optuna trials, refusals dropped to zero,

18
00:00:52,583 --> 00:00:56,496
with a reported KL divergence of 0.0000,

19
00:00:56,496 --> 00:00:58,942
in twelve minutes on CPU.

20
00:00:59,392 --> 00:01:03,926
Full numbers and reproduction steps are on Zenn and GitHub.

21
00:01:03,926 --> 00:01:05,464
Heretic is AGPL-3.0.
